  "description": "INOQIM crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C90 H140 Eu6 N18 O33 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),3.5(C1 H4 O1),8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.547-3.592 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.87-98.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C93.5H170Eu6N20O50.5.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
